 "By convention sweet, by convention bitter, by convention colour. In reality: atoms and void! Ha!": "",
 "Cheerfulness, my friend. A calm soul is a well-arranged soul.": "",
 "Bundles of wood, tied my way. A man is the measure of all things, and the knot is the measure of the bundle.": "",
 "Atoms and Void": "",
 "Democritus: “Cut the cheese in half. And again. And again. Where does it stop?” Click to cut.": "",
 "Democritus: “There must be a smallest piece that cannot be cut. Atomos: uncuttable!”": "",
 "Answer Democritus": "",
 "Keep cutting first.": "",
 "Nico: “Molecules, then atoms, and atoms CAN be cut, into smaller particles still…” Democritus laughs: “Then those are the real atoms!”": "",
 "Democritus of Abdera. Things that have changed what they are made of.": "",
 "Chapter 10 waits in Abdera. Take Captain Nausikles’ ship.": "",
 "Meet the laughing philosopher in the square": "",
 "Ha! A visitor! Come and see, the town has gone wonderfully wrong. A bronze bowl crumbles like bread, salt tastes of honey, and a wall lets people through!": "",
 "He finds it funny. I find it worrying. Their atoms have been rearranged, stranger. Someone is shuffling the very stuff of things.": "",
 "Help me catalogue them! The bowl and the salt first.": "",
 "Examine the bronze bowl": "",
 "Taste the salt": "",
 ", npc: democritus, text: ": "",
 "Atoms and Void: Democritus’ thought experiment": "",
 "Cut the cheese with Democritus": "",
 "Your atoms have parts? Then I was right about the method and wrong about the size. That is the best kind of wrong! Now, the dogs: they smell something sharp in the air. Follow them.": "",
 "The Porous Wall: NOW, the walls are open. Go through!": "",
 "The Dogs Know: follow Argos and Kyon, then pass the porous walls when the lattice pulses": "",
 "They smell ozone. The air after lightning. It’s coming through the walls.": "",
 "The Stranger’s Trail: search the hideout": "",
 "The Stranger’s Trail: go into the hideout": "",
 "Go into the hideout": "",
 "Pick up the book on the table": "",
 "You found the lattice! Wait, before you take it: it could mend our vineyards. They’re rotting. And I could study it for years!": "",
 "Take the lattice. I need it.": "",
 ", npc: leucippus, text: ": "",
 "Heal the vineyards with it first (a day passes).": "",
 "Leave them a working copy made from my phone battery.": "",
 "A matter-filter that rearranged the atoms of things in Abdera, built by the Stranger. Part 10 of 13.": "",
 "Grandpa Leo’s textbook, sixty years older": "",
 "In the Stranger’s hideout in Abdera: Nico’s grandfather’s textbook, aged sixty years. Its table of contents is the list on the machine. Its foreword mentions Diogenes. A margin note in the Socrates chapter: “He’ll need to get out of the house.”": "",
 "Democritus of Abdera": "",
 "The laughing philosopher. With Leucippus he taught that everything is made of tiny indivisible atoms moving in the void. Qualities like sweet, bitter and colour exist “by convention”; in reality there are only atoms and void. His ethics aimed at euthymia, a cheerful calm of the soul.": "",
 "Atomic Lattice recovered: ": "",
 "Clue: the list is the table of contents of Grandpa’s book.": "",
 "Next: Athens. Socrates needs to get out of the house.": "",
 "What is justice? Justice is a shoe that fits, Socrates. Now let go of my sandal.": "",
 "Courage is standing your ground in battle! …What do you mean, “and the soldier who retreats to fight better tomorrow”?": "",
 "I know things! I know my name. I know… is knowing your name knowing something? Mother!": "",
 "The roof doesn’t leak. My husband came home for dinner. Twice. I don’t know who you are, but come again.": "",
 "If you’re one of his friends, you can fix the roof while you wait for him to stop talking.": "",
 "Socrates is the best of us. He is also impossible to get home before dark.": "",
 "Teaching Lamprocles": "",
 "Lamprocles must work out the household money. The family has 7 drachmas. The roofer charges 3 for the tiles, the cousin is owed 2, and bread for the week is 1. How much is left? Use the pebbles: click to move them to the cost piles.": ""
